---

Two fixes on the same screen: the browser extension's panel when it doesn't know the page
you're on.

### The panel offers instead of apologising

Standing on a vacancy freehire doesn't carry yet, the panel used to report a miss — *"No
vacancy"* — with the action tucked underneath. It now leads with the action: **Add this job
in one click**, and a line saying what pressing it gets you (your match score, and a CV you
can tailor for that role).

Same behaviour behind it: freehire imports the posting when it can read the page, and files
the link for a look when it can't.

### SmartRecruiters apply forms resolve to the vacancy

Press **Apply** on a SmartRecruiters posting and you land on a different address — their
one-click form, which identifies the vacancy by a second id that isn't the one in the job's
own URL. The panel didn't recognise it, so it told you freehire had no such vacancy while
showing it on the page behind.

That form now resolves to the posting it belongs to, so the match card follows you from the
job page into the application. Links to SmartRecruiters boards freehire doesn't crawl yet
are also filed under the right employer now, instead of a company name pulled out of their
URL machinery.
